---
globs:
  - "src/agent/triage/**"
  - "src/prWorkspace/writablePrCheckout.ts"
  - "src/agentWork/executors/triageExecutor.ts"
---

Triage run: same-repo only (forks report-only); never force-push, rebase, or amend; push-or-nothing before resolving `fixed` threads; dismissed requires maintainer reply evidence; resolve completed threads (`fixed` after push, `already-resolved`, `dismissed`); leave `skipped` open; use `git commit -n` (hooks off); keep sensitive-path / message / size validation server-side (ADR 0018, ADR 0037). The writable workspace search applies the same normalized sensitive/control-path policy as direct reads and writes, resolves symlink targets before filtering, and omits blocked paths plus matching text. Writable PR checkout must stay isolated from the shared PR repository view cache.
